@module flutter-m13 | Advanced UI
@summary Custom painting, clipping, custom widgets, gestures, drag and drop, theming, accessibility and i18n.

@lesson flutter-m13-l01 | CustomPainter | 8
## Learning objectives
- Draw anything on a canvas

## CustomPainter
CustomPainter gives you a Canvas to draw shapes, paths, text and images. Use it for charts, rings and custom decorations.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class RingPainter extends CustomPainter {
  RingPainter(this.progress);
  final double progress;
  @override
  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {
    final paint = Paint()..style = PaintingStyle.stroke..strokeWidth = 8..color = Colors.indigo;
    canvas.drawArc(Offset.zero & size, -1.57, 6.28 * progress, false, paint);
  }
  @override
  bool shouldRepaint(RingPainter old) => old.progress != progress;
}
```

## Summary
- Return false from shouldRepaint when nothing changed.

@lesson flutter-m13-l02 | CustomClipper | 8
## Learning objectives
- Clip widgets to custom shapes

## CustomClipper
ClipPath with a CustomClipper cuts a widget to any path, for example a wave header.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class WaveClipper extends CustomClipper<Path> {
  @override
  Path getClip(Size s) => Path()
    ..lineTo(0, s.height - 30)
    ..quadraticBezierTo(s.width / 2, s.height, s.width, s.height - 30)
    ..lineTo(s.width, 0)
    ..close();
  @override
  bool shouldReclip(covariant CustomClipper<Path> old) => false;
}
```

## Summary
- ClipPath + CustomClipper for custom shapes.

@lesson flutter-m13-l03 | Custom widgets | 8
## Learning objectives
- Design reusable widget APIs

## Custom widgets
Good custom widgets have clear, named parameters, sensible defaults, const constructors and pull styles from the theme.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class StatTile extends StatelessWidget {
  const StatTile({super.key, required this.label, required this.value, this.icon = Icons.star});
  final String label;
  final String value;
  final IconData icon;
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ListTile(leading: Icon(icon), title: Text(value), subtitle: Text(label));
}
```

## Summary
- Small, themed, const-friendly widgets.

@lesson flutter-m13-l04 | Responsive dashboards | 8
## Learning objectives
- Lay out dashboards for any width

## Responsive dashboards
Combine LayoutBuilder with grids and Wrap so dashboard cards reflow from one column on phones to several on desktop.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget dashboard(List<Widget> cards) => LayoutBuilder(builder: (_, c) {
      final columns = (c.maxWidth / 320).floor().clamp(1, 4);
      return GridView.count(crossAxisCount: columns, children: cards);
    });
```

## Summary
- Derive columns from available width.

@lesson flutter-m13-l05 | Adaptive interfaces | 8
## Learning objectives
- Adapt to platform conventions

## Adaptive interfaces
Adaptive UIs follow each platform's conventions: `Switch.adaptive`, Cupertino dialogs on iOS, keyboard/mouse support on desktop.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget toggle(bool v, ValueChanged<bool> f) => Switch.adaptive(value: v, onChanged: f);
```

## Summary
- Use .adaptive constructors where available.

@lesson flutter-m13-l06 | Complex scrolling | 8
## Learning objectives
- Coordinate nested scroll effects

## Complex scrolling
NestedScrollView coordinates a collapsing header with inner tab lists; ScrollController reads offsets for effects like hiding a FAB.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget nested() => NestedScrollView(
      headerSliverBuilder: (_, __) => const [SliverAppBar(pinned: true, expandedHeight: 120, title: Text('Course'))],
      body: ListView.builder(itemCount: 30, itemBuilder: (_, i) => ListTile(title: Text('Item $i'))),
    );
```

## Summary
- Use slivers and NestedScrollView instead of nesting lists.

@lesson flutter-m13-l07 | Gesture detection | 8
## Learning objectives
- Respond to taps, drags and long presses

## Gesture detection
GestureDetector recognises taps, double taps, long presses, pans and scales. InkWell adds Material ripples.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget card() => GestureDetector(
      onDoubleTap: () => debugPrint('liked'),
      onLongPress: () => debugPrint('menu'),
      child: const Card(child: Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(24), child: Text('Double tap me'))),
    );
```

## Summary
- Prefer InkWell for Material tap feedback.

@lesson flutter-m13-l08 | Drag and drop | 8
## Learning objectives
- Move items between targets

## Drag and drop
Draggable and DragTarget implement drag and drop; ReorderableListView reorders list items.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget reorder(List<String> items, void Function(int, int) onReorder) => ReorderableListView(
      onReorder: onReorder,
      children: [for (final i in items) ListTile(key: ValueKey(i), title: Text(i))],
    );
```

## Summary
- Reorderable items need keys.

@lesson flutter-m13-l09 | Advanced theming | 8
## Learning objectives
- Extend the theme with your own tokens

## Advanced theming
ThemeExtension adds custom design tokens (brand gradients, spacing) to ThemeData with lerp support for animated theme changes.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class Brand extends ThemeExtension<Brand> {
  const Brand(this.accent);
  final Color accent;
  @override
  Brand copyWith({Color? accent}) => Brand(accent ?? this.accent);
  @override
  Brand lerp(Brand? other, double t) => Brand(Color.lerp(accent, other?.accent, t)!);
}
```

## Summary
- Read with Theme.of(context).extension<Brand>().

@lesson flutter-m13-l10 | Accessibility | 8
## Learning objectives
- Build for screen readers and large text

## Accessibility
Use Semantics, labels on icons, logical focus order, contrast ≥ 4.5:1 and test with TalkBack, VoiceOver and 200% text size.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget avatar() => Semantics(label: 'Profile picture of Ada', image: true, child: const CircleAvatar(child: Text('A')));
```

## Summary
- Every interactive element needs a label.

@lesson flutter-m13-l11 | Internationalization | 8
## Learning objectives
- Translate your app

## Internationalization
Use `flutter_localizations` and ARB files with `flutter gen-l10n` to generate a typed `AppLocalizations` class; format dates/numbers with intl.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

// l10n.yaml: arb-dir: lib/l10n, template-arb-file: app_en.arb
// Text(AppLocalizations.of(context)!.helloWorld)
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Never hard-code user-facing strings.
